.TH PEEK-THUMBNAILER 1 "2026-09-07" "peek" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
peek-thumbnailer \- generate file manager thumbnails with peek's decoders
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B peek-thumbnailer
.I INPUT
.I OUTPUT.png
.I SIZE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B peek-thumbnailer
implements the freedesktop thumbnailer contract using the same decoders
.BR peek (1)
previews files with, so the icon in the file manager and the preview over it
cannot disagree about what a file looks like.
.PP
It is not normally run by hand. A
.I .thumbnailer
entry in
.I /usr/share/thumbnailers/
registers it, and the file manager's thumbnail factory invokes it, substituting
the input path, an output path, and the size.
.PP
.I INPUT
may be a path or a
.I file://
URI.
.I SIZE
is the longest edge in pixels.
.PP
Files whose best representation is not a picture \(em text, archives,
directories \(em exit non-zero without writing anything. That is the
contract's way of saying the file manager's own type icon is the better
answer, and is not an error.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
A thumbnail was written.
.TP
.B 1
No thumbnail applies, or the file could not be read or decoded.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR peek (1)
